    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d255">

                <pb facs="0770" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">871.01/12–2345</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bevin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-23">December 23,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear James</hi>: After listening to the discussions
                    of the last few days on the subject of the Balkan States, which is of so great
                    importance to all of us, I have come to the conclusion that there is possibility
                    of agreement between our three Delegations.</p>
                <p>I enclose the draft of a memorandum embodying my ideas, on which I hope we may
                    agree. I trust that you will find this acceptable, and that on this basis we can
                    reach agreement in one Conference.</p>
                <p>I am sending a similiar letter to M. Molotov.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ernest Bevin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d255-a1.xml" xpointer="d255-a1"/>
